          "path": "_m/9/v/6/k/driskill-hotel-wp/driskill-hotel-austin-texas-hi.jpg",
          "filename": "Driskill Hotel, Austin, Texas Historical Marker (8511756246).jpg",
          "caption": "Built 1885-86 by Col. Jesse L. Driskill (1824-1890), cattle king who moved to Austin in 1869. Brick dressed with limestone. Had three grand entrances -- one the largest arched doorway in Texas. \"Ladies' Entrance\" was on northeast. Bust of Col. Driskill is over south arch, busts of his rancher sons on east and west. Rich furnishings were selected by Col. Driskill, who leased out his hotel -- Southwest's finest when it opened, Christmas 1886. Recorded Texas Historic Landmark - 1966",
          "alt": "Built 1885-86 by Col. Jesse L. Driskill (1824-1890), cattle king who moved to Austin in 1869. Brick dressed with limestone. Had three grand entrances -- one the largest arched doorway in Texas. \"Ladies' Entrance\" was on northeast. Bust of Col. Driskill is over south arch, busts of his rancher sons on east and west. Rich furnishings were selected by Col. Driskill, who leased out his hotel -- Southwest's finest when it opened, Christmas 1886. Recorded Texas Historic Landmark - 1966",
          "width": 3456,
          "height": 5184,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Nicolas Henderson from Coppell, Texas",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Driskill_Hotel,_Austin,_Texas_Historical_Marker_(8511756246).jpg",
